{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AAO REVIEWS - page bootstrap
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid. Emits the widget stylesheet, the engine and the runtime
config. The engine bails out immediately (and fetches nothing) on pages that hold neither a
`.aao-reviews` widget nor a `.aao-rating` badge, so this is cheap sitewide.

Data is split across assets so no page downloads the whole corpus, and so a review set shared by
many products is stored once:

  aao-reviews-summary.json     one row per handle (~36KB). Fetched once per page that renders a
                               rating badge or the widget. Its `src` names the asset below that
                               holds each handle's review list.
  aao-reviews-store.json       the store-wide showcase set Loox served on products with no reviews
                               of their own.
  aao-reviews-set-<hash>.json  the other shared review sets.
  aao-reviews-p-<handle>.json  products that have a review set of their own.
  aao-rev-<name>.jpg           review photos, re-hosted off the Loox CDN.

All of these are produced from the harvest by docs/reviews/split_reviews.py.

Endpoints live on the agency VPS:
  submitUrl    POST {handle, rating, author, email, text} -> {"ok": true}
  approvedUrl  GET  the same products-map schema as the harvest, merged over the baked data

Set `inline_summary: true` when rendering to embed the summary in the page instead of fetching it.
That removes a request on every page at the cost of ~16KB of HTML sitewide, so it is off by
default. See docs/reviews/README.md.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  PARITY vs HONESTY - the one switch worth knowing about.

  Loox padded this catalogue: of 262 products showing reviews, only 11 have a review actually
  written about them. The other 251 display a shared "showcase" feed Loox injected. Everything
  here defaults to reproducing that exactly, so cancelling the app changes nothing a customer can
  see.

  Set genuine_only below to true and every product shows only its own reviews instead. On today's
  data that means 11 products with reviews and 251 showing "Be the first to review this product".
  It is a business decision, not a technical one. See docs/reviews/README.md.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign genuine_only = false

  assign submit_url = 'https://allign.agency/aao/reviews/submit'
  assign approved_url = 'https://allign.agency/aao/reviews/approved.json'

  comment
    The theme's asset directory, e.g. https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/.../assets/ - the engine
    builds the review-list and photo URLs from it rather than hard-coding a CDN host.
  endcomment
  assign asset_base = 'aao-reviews.css' | asset_url | split: 'aao-reviews.css' | first
-%}

{{ 'aao-reviews.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<script>
  window.AAO_REVIEWS_CONFIG = {
    assetBase: {{ asset_base | json }},
    summaryUrl: {{ 'aao-reviews-summary.json' | asset_url | json }},
    submitUrl: {{ submit_url | json }},
    approvedUrl: {{ approved_url | json }},
    genuineOnly: {{ genuine_only | json }}
  };
</script>

{%- if inline_summary -%}
  <script type="application/json" id="aao-reviews-summary-data">{{ 'aao-reviews-summary.json' | inline_asset_content }}</script>
{%- endif -%}

<script src="{{ 'aao-reviews.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
